Subject: [PATCH 01/12] =?UTF-8?q?feat(schema):=20Alembic=20owns=20the=20wh?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ole=20schema=20=E2=80=94=20legacy=20baseline,=20drift=20gate,?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20no=20DDL=20in=20workers?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Until now three layers built the database: `Base.metadata.create_all` for
forty "legacy" tables, `db_migrate.apply_schema_column_patches` adding
whatever columns the ORM had grown, and the Alembic chain for the Agent
Platform — and every uvicorn worker ran the first two at boot behind an
advisory lock. The ORM was the schema's source of truth and nothing checked
that the chain could rebuild it.

- New chain root `0000a1b2c3d4_legacy_schema_baseline`: the forty legacy
  tables as a frozen autogenerate rendering (guarded by `if name not in
  existing`). `31adeeec2bce` now revises it. A fresh database gets every
  table from `alembic upgrade head` alone; an installation at any later
  revision has the baseline as an ancestor and never runs it.
- `4b0c1d2e3f4a_align_platform_schema_with_orm`: nine ORM indexes on
  Alembic-owned tables that no revision ever created (the column patch
  skipped those tables), and `*_memory_events.detail` JSON -> JSONB.
- ORM aligned with what the chain really builds: the deferred FKs
  (chat_sessions -> agents/agent_versions/projects, chat_messages ->
  agent_runs, request_logs/image_attempts/video_jobs -> projects) are
  declared with `use_alter`; governance `event_hash` is a named unique
  constraint plus a lookup index; `project_resources.project_id` index
  carries the migration's name; a duplicate unique on
  `project_invitations.token_hash` and a duplicate index on
  `project_resources.uploaded_by_user_id` are gone.
- `python -m app.migrate`: `alembic upgrade head` first, then — while
  `LEGACY_SCHEMA_BOOTSTRAP` (new, default true for one release) is on — the
  create_all/column catch-up for installations that predate the baseline,
  then validation. `app.main` lifespan runs no DDL any more; a worker only
  validates the schema and refuses to start on mismatch.
- `tests/test_schema_baseline.py` (Postgres canary job): scratch database,
  `alembic upgrade head`, `compare_metadata` must be empty. This is what
  turns every future ORM change into a required revision.

Verified: fresh Postgres via chain only -> 0 drift; a database built the
old way (create_all + chain at a3b4c5d6e7f8) upgraded with the new migrate
-> head, 0 drift; the same on SQLite; fresh DB with the bootstrap flag off
-> validation passes; 1371 tests; mypy/vulture/ruff clean.

